=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
No fault exists in this network. Every component of the data path between pc1 (195.11.14.2) and pc2 (200.1.1.2) was inspected and found fully operational. Both router1 (AS 1) and router2 (AS 2) have their eBGP session established and stable (uptime ~3 minutes). Each router correctly receives one prefix from its peer — 200.1.1.0/24 on router1 and 195.11.14.0/24 on router2 — and both are installed as active FIB entries (marked `B>*`). All four interfaces (eth0/eth1 on each router, eth0 on each host) are UP with correct IP addresses. Firewall tables on all four devices are completely open (default ACCEPT, no rules). A live end-to-end ping from pc1 to pc2 transmitted four packets and received four back with zero loss and sub-3 ms round-trip time. The FRR configurations are minimal and correct — no inbound or outbound route filters, no route-maps, no prefix-lists that could suppress reachability. The BGP re-advertisement of learned prefixes (PfxSnt=2) is harmless; peers reject them via AS-PATH loop detection as designed. The reported symptom — partner machine completely unreachable — cannot be reproduced at this moment. The network is healthy; the incident appears to be a transient or user-side issue that self-resolved before investigation began.
=== END ===
```